        "id": 5572,
        "name": "broccoli",
        "username": "broccoli",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/{size}/1861_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-03T22:33:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was curious about the section of the card that says “If the played card is limited card already in play, discard that card an play the next card.”  My question is whether that is intended to be performed exactly once (the literal reading of the card), or if it is intended to be repeated until a non-“limited and in play” card is played?</p>\n<p>thanks,<br>\nBroccoli</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:15.782Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 3,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 10.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 5570,
        "topic_slug": "atlantean-font-of-power",
        "display_username": "broccoli",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
