      {
        "id": 26645,
        "name": "TheJayMann",
        "username": "TheJayMann",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-03T22:36:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My guess is that it’s intended to be repeated as necessary, as doing it once would mean that you follow the last part about playing the card, causing two limited cards to be in play.  As far as I can tell, there is no ruling about what to do if a situation occurs which creates multiple limited cards in play, only that it’s not to be allowed to begin with.  This would leave the previous result undefined if it were only to occur once.</p>\n<p>Short answer: repeat.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:00:35.402Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 5570,
        "topic_slug": "atlantean-font-of-power",
